From: Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra Ubuntu port <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spa: libcamera: skip array controls in the legacy mapper

libcamera controls retain their scalar element type when the value is an
array. The PipeWire 1.0.5 SPA mapper only supports scalar controls, but used
the element type alone and called ControlValue::get<T>() on arrays such as
ColourGains. With libcamera 0.7 this correctly asserts and aborts PipeWire as
soon as a camera node is exported.

Do not advertise array controls until the SPA mapper supports their shape.
They remain managed internally by libcamera (including AWB colour gains).
---
 spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-utils.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-utils.cpp b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-utils.cpp
index 818e70c756ba..bcad7fc233b6 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-utils.cpp
+++ b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-utils.cpp
@@ -508,6 +508,9 @@ spa_libcamera_enum_controls(struct impl *impl, struct port *port, int seq,
 			SPA_PROP_INFO_description, SPA_POD_String(ctrl_id->name().c_str()),
 			0);
 
+	if (ctrl_id->isArray())
+		goto next;
+
 	switch (ctrl_id->type()) {
 	case ControlTypeBool: {
 		bool def;
-- 
